IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa2-common`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11: the general protections and sham arrangements (Part 3-1).
--
-- SEAT: the person action was taken against -- the employee, the job applicant, the independent contractor -- who asks
-- "Was what they did to me adverse action? Was it unlawful? Was I misled into being a contractor? By when must I act,
-- and when can I go to court?"
--
-- PROVISIONS. s 340 (protection of workplace rights), s 341 (workplace right; prospective employees and the s 341(4),
-- (5) exceptions), s 342 items 1-4 with s 342(2)-(4) (adverse action), s 351 (discrimination, with the s 351(2)
-- exceptions), s 352 with reg 3.01 (dismissal for temporary absence through illness or injury), ss 357-359 (sham
-- contracting), ss 359B, 359C (sham casual employment), s 360 (multiple reasons), s 361 (reason presumed unless
-- proved otherwise), ss 365, 366 (dismissal disputes: 21 days), s 369(1)(c) (14 days to agree to arbitration), s 370
-- (14 days to go to court), s 372 (non-dismissal disputes). Out: the industrial activity protections (ss 346-350B),
-- coercion and undue influence (ss 343-345, 355), ss 353-354, 356, 362-364; items 3A, 4A, 5-8 of the s 342 table (the
-- platform operator's and the industrial association's adverse action, and action against an employer); application
-- fees (ss 367, 373 with regs 3.02, 3.03); ss 727-734 (one claim only).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 73 (register id C2026C00355), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00028.txt;
-- Fair Work Regulations 2009, Compilation No. 57 (register id F2026C00996), reg 3.01, as deposited at
-- ../../../fair-work-regulations-2009/registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt. BASELINE; see NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- the general protections, from the seat of the person action was taken against`

§§ `s 341 -- do I have a workplace right`

-- s 341(1): "A person has a workplace right if the person: (a) is entitled to the benefit of, or has a role or
-- responsibility under, a workplace law, workplace instrument or order made by an industrial body; or (b) is able to
-- initiate, or participate in, a process or proceedings under a workplace law or workplace instrument; or (c) is able
-- to make a complaint or inquiry: (i) to a person or body having the capacity under a workplace law to seek compliance
-- ...; or (ii) if the person is an employee--in relation to his or her employment."
-- s 341(3): "A prospective employee is taken to have the workplace rights he or she would have if he or she were
-- employed in the prospective employment" -- so a job applicant answers the same facts as if employed.
@export Do I have a workplace right (s 341)?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a benefit under a workplace law, award, agreement or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the benefit of (or have a role under) a workplace law, award, enterprise agreement or Fair Work Commission order -- for example, pay, leave or a flexible working request (as a job applicant, answer as if you had the job)
      `I can start or take part in a process or proceedings under a workplace law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to start or take part in a process or proceedings under a workplace law or instrument (an FWC conference, court proceedings, bargaining, dispute settlement, a flexible work request)
      `I can complain to a body that enforces workplace law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to complain or inquire to a body that can seek compliance with a workplace law (for example the Fair Work Ombudsman)
      `I am an employee able to complain about my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an employee able to make a complaint or inquiry about your employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a workplace right` IF
        `I am entitled to a benefit under a workplace law, award, agreement or order`
    OR  `I can start or take part in a process or proceedings under a workplace law`
    OR  `I can complain to a body that enforces workplace law`
    OR  `I am an employee able to complain about my employment`

§§ `s 342 -- was it adverse action`

-- s 342(1), table items 1 to 4 -- adverse action taken by
--   1 an employer against an employee: "(a) dismisses the employee; or (b) injures the employee in his or her
--     employment; or (c) alters the position of the employee to the employee's prejudice; or (d) discriminates between
--     the employee and other employees of the employer";
--   2 a prospective employer against a prospective employee: "(a) refuses to employ ...; or (b) discriminates against
--     the prospective employee in the terms or conditions on which the prospective employer offers to employ";
--   3 a principal against an independent contractor: "(a) terminates the contract; or (b) injures the independent
--     contractor in relation to the terms and conditions of the contract; or (c) alters the position of the
--     independent contractor to the independent contractor's prejudice; or (d) refuses to make use of ... services
--     offered ...; or (e) refuses to supply ... goods or services";
--   4 a principal proposing to engage an independent contractor: "(a) refuses to engage ...; or (b) discriminates
--     against the independent contractor in the terms or conditions on which the principal offers to engage ...; or (c)
--     refuses to make use of ... services offered ...; or (d) refuses to supply ... goods or services".
-- s 342(2): adverse action "includes: (a) threatening to take action covered by the table ...; and (b) organising
-- such action." s 342(3): it "does not include action that is authorised by or under: (a) this Act or any other law of
-- the Commonwealth; or (b) a law of a State or Territory prescribed by the regulations." s 342(4)(a): nor an employer
-- standing down an employee engaged in protected industrial action under a contract that provides for it.
DECLARE `Who I am to them` IS ONE OF
    `their employee`
    `someone applying to be their employee`
    `an independent contractor they engaged`
    `an independent contractor they proposed to engage`

DECLARE `What they did` IS ONE OF
    `dismissed me or ended my contract`
    `injured me in my employment or contract`
    `altered my position to my prejudice`
    `treated me differently from their other employees`
    `refused to employ or engage me`
    `offered me worse terms than others`
    `refused to use services I offered`
    `refused to supply goods or services to me`
    `something else`

GIVEN `who I am to them` IS A `Who I am to them`, `what they did` IS A `What they did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 342 table covers it` IS
    CONSIDER `who I am to them`
    WHEN `their employee` THEN
        CONSIDER `what they did`
        WHEN `dismissed me or ended my contract` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `injured me in my employment or contract` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `altered my position to my prejudice` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `treated me differently from their other employees` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `someone applying to be their employee` THEN
        CONSIDER `what they did`
        WHEN `refused to employ or engage me` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `offered me worse terms than others` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `an independent contractor they engaged` THEN
        CONSIDER `what they did`
        WHEN `dismissed me or ended my contract` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `injured me in my employment or contract` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `altered my position to my prejudice` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `refused to use services I offered` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `refused to supply goods or services to me` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `an independent contractor they proposed to engage` THEN
        CONSIDER `what they did`
        WHEN `refused to employ or engage me` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `offered me worse terms than others` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `refused to use services I offered` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `refused to supply goods or services to me` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Was what they did (or threatened or organised) to me adverse action (s 342)?
GIVEN `who I am to them` IS A `Who I am to them` @desc Who you are to the person who acted: their employee; someone applying to be their employee; an independent contractor they engaged; or an independent contractor they proposed to engage
      `what they did` IS A `What they did` @desc What they did, threatened or organised: dismissed you or ended your contract; injured you in your employment or contract; altered your position to your prejudice; treated you differently from their other employees; refused to employ or engage you; offered you worse terms than others; refused to use services you offered; refused to supply goods or services to you; or something else
      `a Commonwealth law or prescribed State law authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was authorised by the Fair Work Act, another Commonwealth law, or a State or Territory law the Regulations prescribe
      `it was a stand down during protected industrial action that my contract allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was your employer standing you down while you were in protected industrial action, under a contract term that provides for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it adverse action` IF
        `the s 342 table covers it` `who I am to them` `what they did`
    AND (NOT `a Commonwealth law or prescribed State law authorised it`)
    AND (NOT `it was a stand down during protected industrial action that my contract allows`)

§§ `ss 340, 360, 361 -- was it taken because of my workplace right`

-- s 340(1): "A person must not take adverse action against another person: (a) because the other person: (i) has a
-- workplace right; or (ii) has, or has not, exercised a workplace right; or (iii) proposes or proposes not to ...
-- exercise a workplace right; or (b) to prevent the exercise of a workplace right by the other person."
-- s 360: "a person takes action for a particular reason if the reasons for the action include that reason."
-- s 361(1): if it is alleged that action was taken for a particular reason and that would be a contravention, "it is
-- presumed that the action was ... taken for that reason ... unless the person proves otherwise"; (2) not for interim
-- injunctions. The person who acted must prove it: whether they did is the court's finding, an INPUT.
-- s 341(4), (5): a prospective employer does not contravene s 340(1) by (4) making an offer "conditional on the
-- prospective employee accepting a guarantee of annual earnings", or (5) refusing to employ because the person "would
-- be entitled to the benefit of Part 2-8 or 6-3A" (transfer of business).
@export Did they break the general protections by taking adverse action against me because of my workplace right (ss 340, 360, 361)?
GIVEN `it was adverse action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was done was adverse action (ask the s 342 question first)
      `I have a workplace right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a workplace right (ask the s 341 question first)
      `I say my workplace right was among their reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say they acted because you had, used, did not use, or proposed to use a workplace right, or to stop you using it (one reason among others is enough)
      `they prove it was not among their reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they prove to the court that your workplace right was not one of their reasons
      `it was only an offer conditional on a guarantee of annual earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a job applicant: whether the action was only making the job offer conditional on your accepting a guarantee of annual earnings
      `it was only refusing me because of transfer of business rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a job applicant: whether they refused to employ you only because you would be entitled to transfer of business protections (Parts 2-8, 6-3A)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did they break s 340` IF
        `it was adverse action`
    AND `I have a workplace right`
    AND `I say my workplace right was among their reasons`
    AND (NOT `they prove it was not among their reasons`)
    AND (NOT `it was only an offer conditional on a guarantee of annual earnings`)
    AND (NOT `it was only refusing me because of transfer of business rights`)

§§ `s 351 -- discrimination`

-- s 351(1): "An employer must not take adverse action against a person who is an employee, or prospective employee, of
-- the employer because of the person's race, colour, sex, sexual orientation, breastfeeding, gender identity, intersex
-- status, age, physical or mental disability, marital status, family or carer's responsibilities, subjection to family
-- and domestic violence, pregnancy, religion, political opinion, national extraction or social origin."
-- s 351(2): it "does not apply to action that is: (a) not unlawful under any anti-discrimination law in force in the
-- place where the action is taken; or (b) taken because of the inherent requirements of the particular position
-- concerned; or (c) if the action is taken against a staff member of an institution conducted in accordance with the
-- doctrines ... of a particular religion or creed--taken: (i) in good faith; and (ii) to avoid injury to the religious
-- susceptibilities of adherents". s 351(3) lists the anti-discrimination laws (the four Commonwealth Acts and one in
-- each State and Territory); whether the action is unlawful under one is an INPUT.
DECLARE `Protected attribute` IS ONE OF
    `race`, `colour`, `sex`, `sexual orientation`, `breastfeeding`, `gender identity`, `intersex status`, `age`
    `physical or mental disability`, `marital status`, `family or carer's responsibilities`
    `subjection to family and domestic violence`, `pregnancy`, `religion`, `political opinion`, `national extraction`
    `social origin`, `none of these`

@export Did my employer break s 351 by taking adverse action against me because of a protected attribute?
GIVEN `who I am to them` IS A `Who I am to them` @desc Who you are to the person who acted: their employee; someone applying to be their employee; or an independent contractor (s 351 protects only employees and job applicants)
      `it was adverse action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was done was adverse action (ask the s 342 question first)
      `the attribute` IS A `Protected attribute` @desc The attribute you say was among their reasons (race, colour, sex, sexual orientation, breastfeeding, gender identity, intersex status, age, disability, marital status, family or carer's responsibilities, family and domestic violence, pregnancy, religion, political opinion, national extraction, social origin), or none of these
      `they prove it was not among their reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they prove to the court that the attribute was not one of their reasons (s 361)
      `the action is unlawful under an anti-discrimination law where it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is unlawful under an anti-discrimination law in force where it was taken (the Commonwealth Age, Disability, Racial or Sex Discrimination Act, or your State or Territory's equivalent)
      `it was because of the inherent requirements of the position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was taken because of the inherent requirements of the particular position
      `it was a religious institution acting in good faith to avoid injury to religious susceptibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are on the staff of a religious institution, whether it acted in good faith to avoid injury to the religious susceptibilities of adherents
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did they break s 351` IF
        `I am an employee or job applicant`
    AND `it was adverse action`
    AND `an attribute is named`
    AND (NOT `they prove it was not among their reasons`)
    AND `the action is unlawful under an anti-discrimination law where it happened`
    AND (NOT `it was because of the inherent requirements of the position`)
    AND (NOT `it was a religious institution acting in good faith to avoid injury to religious susceptibilities`)
    WHERE
        `I am an employee or job applicant` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who I am to them`
            WHEN `their employee` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `someone applying to be their employee` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `an attribute is named` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the attribute`
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 352 with reg 3.01 -- dismissed while off sick or injured`

-- s 352: "An employer must not dismiss an employee because the employee is temporarily absent from work because of
-- illness or injury of a kind prescribed by the regulations."
-- reg 3.01(2): prescribed if the employee "provides a medical certificate ... or a statutory declaration ... within: (a)
-- 24 hours after the commencement of the absence; or (b) such longer period as is reasonable"; (3) or is required by a
-- workplace instrument to notify and substantiate the absence and "complies with those terms"; (4) or has given the
-- evidence s 107(3)(a) requires for paid personal/carer's leave for personal illness or injury.
-- reg 3.01(5): not prescribed if "(a) either: (i) the employee's absence extends for more than 3 months; or (ii) the
-- total absences of the employee, within a 12 month period, have been more than 3 months ...; and (b) the employee is
-- not on paid personal/carer's leave ... for the duration of the absence." reg 3.01(6): paid personal/carer's leave
-- "does not include a period when the employee is absent from work while receiving compensation under" a workers'
-- compensation law.
@export Was I unlawfully dismissed for being temporarily off work sick or injured (s 352, reg 3.01)?
GIVEN `I was dismissed because I was off work sick or injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were dismissed because you were absent from work because of illness or injury (one reason among others is enough, and the employer must prove otherwise)
      `I gave a medical certificate or statutory declaration in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a medical certificate or statutory declaration within 24 hours of the absence starting, or within a longer period that was reasonable
      `I followed my award or agreement's rules for notifying and proving the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award or agreement required you to notify and substantiate the absence and you did
      `I gave the evidence needed for paid sick leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your employer the evidence required to take paid personal (sick) leave for the illness or injury
      `months this absence has lasted` IS A NUMBER @desc How long this absence had lasted when you were dismissed, in months
      `months of absence in the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total absences for illness or injury within the 12 months before the dismissal, in months
      `I was on paid sick leave for the whole absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were on paid personal (sick) leave for the whole of the absence
      `I received workers compensation during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were receiving workers' compensation for any of the absence (those periods do not count as paid sick leave)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I unlawfully dismissed for being off sick` IF
        `I was dismissed because I was off work sick or injured`
    AND `my illness or injury is of a prescribed kind`
    WHERE
        `my illness or injury is of a prescribed kind` MEANS
                (   `I gave a medical certificate or statutory declaration in time`
                 OR `I followed my award or agreement's rules for notifying and proving the absence`
                 OR `I gave the evidence needed for paid sick leave`)
            AND (NOT `the absence is too long`)
        `the absence is too long` MEANS
                (`months this absence has lasted` GREATER THAN 3 OR `months of absence in the last 12 months` GREATER THAN 3)
            AND (NOT (`I was on paid sick leave for the whole absence` AND (NOT `I received workers compensation during the absence`)))

§§ `ss 357-359C -- sham contracting and sham casual employment`

-- s 357(1): an employer "that employs, or proposes to employ, an individual must not represent to the individual that
-- the contract of employment ... is a contract for services under which the individual performs ... work as an
-- independent contractor." s 357(2): not if "the employer proves that, when the representation was made, the employer
-- reasonably believed that the contract was a contract for services"; (3) regard must be had to "the size and nature of
-- the employer's enterprise". Whether the arrangement is in truth employment is the s 15AA question -- an INPUT.
@export Did my employer break the sham contracting rule by telling me I was a contractor when I was an employee (s 357)?
GIVEN `I am in truth their employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, looking at the real substance of the relationship, you are (or would be) their employee rather than an independent contractor
      `they told me my contract was a contract for services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they represented to you that you are (or would be) working as an independent contractor under a contract for services
      `they prove they reasonably believed it was a contract for services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they prove they reasonably believed, when they said it, that it was a contract for services (the court considers the size and nature of their business)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did they break s 357` IF
        `I am in truth their employee or prospective employee`
    AND `they told me my contract was a contract for services`
    AND (NOT `they prove they reasonably believed it was a contract for services`)

-- s 358: an employer "must not dismiss, or threaten to dismiss, an individual who: (a) is an employee of the employer;
-- and (b) performs particular work for the employer; in order to engage the individual as an independent contractor to
-- perform the same, or substantially the same, work under a contract for services." s 359B: the same, "in order to
-- engage the individual as a casual employee".
@export Was I dismissed (or threatened with dismissal) so I could be taken back as a contractor or a casual (ss 358, 359B)?
GIVEN `I was their employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were their employee doing particular work for them
      `they dismissed me or threatened to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they dismissed you or threatened to dismiss you
      `it was to re-engage me for the same or substantially the same work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they did it in order to engage you to do the same, or substantially the same, work as an independent contractor (s 358) or as a casual employee (s 359B)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I dismissed to be re-engaged` IF
        `I was their employee`
    AND `they dismissed me or threatened to`
    AND `it was to re-engage me for the same or substantially the same work`

-- s 359: an employer that "employs, or has at any time employed, an individual to perform particular work must not make a
-- statement that the employer knows is false in order to persuade or influence the individual to enter into a contract
-- for services under which the individual will perform, as an independent contractor, the same, or substantially the
-- same, work". s 359C: the same, for someone employed "other than as a casual employee", to persuade them into "a
-- contract for casual employment" (two lettered paragraphs, same elements).
DECLARE `Re-engaged as` IS ONE OF `an independent contractor`, `a casual employee`

@export Did my employer knowingly lie to persuade me to become a contractor or a casual for the same work (ss 359, 359C)?
GIVEN `they employ or employed me for particular work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they employ you, or have at any time employed you, to do particular work
      `the new basis` IS A `Re-engaged as` @desc What they wanted you to become: an independent contractor, or a casual employee
      `I was employed other than as a casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed other than as a casual (needed only where they wanted you to become a casual)
      `they made a statement they knew was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they made a statement they knew was false
      `it was to persuade me onto the new basis for the same work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement was made to persuade or influence you to take a contract on the new basis for the same, or substantially the same, work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did they lie to change my basis` IF
        `they employ or employed me for particular work`
    AND `the old basis qualifies`
    AND `they made a statement they knew was false`
    AND `it was to persuade me onto the new basis for the same work`
    WHERE
        `the old basis qualifies` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the new basis`
            WHEN `an independent contractor` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a casual employee` THEN `I was employed other than as a casual`

§§ `ss 365, 366, 369, 370 -- a dismissal: the FWC first, then court` -- situation: only if you were dismissed

-- s 365: a person who "alleges that the person was dismissed in contravention of this Part" may apply to the FWC.
-- s 366(1): the application "must be made: (a) within 21 days after the alleged dismissal took effect; or (b) within
-- such further period as the FWC allows under subsection (2)"; (2) "if the FWC is satisfied that there are exceptional
-- circumstances" (reason for delay, action taken to dispute, prejudice to the employer, merits, fairness) -- an INPUT.
@export By when must I apply to the FWC about a dismissal I say broke the general protections (s 366(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my dismissal took effect on` IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took effect
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply about my general protections dismissal` MEANS
    `the day that is` `my dismissal took effect on` 21

@export Is my FWC application about a general protections dismissal in time (s 366)?
GIVEN `my dismissal took effect on` IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took effect
      `I apply on` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge (or lodged) the application with the FWC
      `the FWC allows a further period for exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are late, whether the FWC is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances and allows you a further period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my general protections dismissal application in time` IF
        `falls on or before` `I apply on` (`By when must I apply about my general protections dismissal` `my dismissal took effect on`)
    OR  `the FWC allows a further period for exceptional circumstances`

-- s 369(1): the FWC may arbitrate if it has issued a s 368(3)(a) certificate (all reasonable attempts to resolve the
-- dispute have been or are likely to be unsuccessful) and "the parties notify the FWC that they agree", the notice
-- "given to the FWC within 14 days after the day the certificate is issued, or within such period as the FWC allows".
@export By when must my employer and I tell the FWC that we agree to arbitration of my dismissal dispute (s 369(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the certificate was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The day the FWC issued its certificate that attempts to resolve the dispute have failed
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must we agree to arbitration of my dismissal dispute` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the certificate was issued on` 14

-- s 370: a person entitled to apply under s 365 "must not make a general protections court application ... unless: (a)
-- both ... (i) the FWC has issued a certificate under paragraph 368(3)(a) ...; (ii) the ... application is made within
-- 14 days after the day the certificate is issued, or within such period as the court allows ...; or (b) the ...
-- application includes an application for an interim injunction."
@export By when must I start court proceedings about my dismissal after the FWC's certificate (s 370(a)(ii))?
GIVEN `the certificate was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The day the FWC issued its certificate that attempts to resolve the dispute have failed
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I go to court about my dismissal` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the certificate was issued on` 14

-- Notes 1 to ss 369 and 370: once the parties agree to arbitration, ss 727 and 728 "generally" bar a court application.
-- Those sections are not encoded: where the parties have agreed to arbitration the answer is NOTHING.
@export Can I take my general protections dismissal dispute to court (s 370)?
GIVEN `the FWC issued a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FWC has issued its certificate that attempts to resolve the dispute have failed
      `the certificate was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The day the certificate was issued (any date if there is none)
      `I file in court on` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or filed) the court application
      `the court allows a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are late, whether the court allows you a longer period
      `my application includes an interim injunction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your court application includes an application for an interim injunction (for example, to stop the dismissal taking effect)
      `we agreed to FWC arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer notified the FWC that you agree to it arbitrating the dispute
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I take my dismissal dispute to court` MEANS
    IF `we agreed to FWC arbitration`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (   (    `the FWC issued a certificate`
                   AND (   `falls on or before` `I file in court on` (`By when must I go to court about my dismissal` `the certificate was issued on`)
                        OR `the court allows a longer period`))
               OR `my application includes an interim injunction`)

-- s 372: "If: (a) a person alleges a contravention of this Part; and (b) the person is not entitled to apply to the FWC
-- under section 365 ...; the person may apply to the FWC under this section". The s 370 limit does not apply to such a
-- dispute; the s 544 six-year limit for court proceedings (encoded in baseline-2026-10) does.
@export Can I ask the FWC to deal with a general protections dispute that is not about a dismissal (s 372)?
GIVEN `I allege a general protections contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say someone broke a general protection (Part 3-1) against you
      `I was dismissed because of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say you were dismissed in breach of the general protections (then you use the dismissal route, s 365)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask the FWC about a non-dismissal dispute` IF
        `I allege a general protections contravention`
    AND (NOT `I was dismissed because of it`)
